{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794229116,"nonce":"42x3ov4Aalbi0o6nk5hcEjOoRtA=","title":"Dragging a resizable handle beside a flexible panel jumps","message":"The drag starts from each panel's stored size signal. A flexible panel's size\nlives only in layout; its signal keeps the 200 px default. With a minimum on\nthe flexible panel, the clamp `right_start - delta \u003e= right_min` used 200 and\nthrew the fixed panel to `left + 200 - right_min`. In the russl toy, dragging\nthe sidebar handle right by 50 px collapsed the sidebar to ~66 px.\n\nFix: each panel carries a `DivRef`; mouse-down reads the laid-out sizes,\nfalling back to the stored size before layout. Test\n`a_drag_beside_a_flexible_panel_starts_from_its_laid_out_size`.","files":null}]}